{"prompt":"Write a JavaScript program to list files in the current directory","intent":"write_program","content":"Here is a minimal JavaScript list files in the current directory program:\n\n```javascript\nconst fs = require(\"fs\");\n\nconst names = fs\n  .readdirSync(\".\")\n  .filter((name) => fs.statSync(name).isFile())\n  .sort();\n\nfor (const name of names) {\n  console.log(name);\n}\n```\n\nExecution status: not run - the browser sandbox has no filesystem access for this javascript program.\n\nCopy the snippet into a javascript environment to verify.\n\nThe sample output below is for a clean directory containing exactly `README.md`, `data.txt` and `main.js` and no extra files:\n```text\nREADME.md\ndata.txt\nmain.js\n```\n\nHow it works:\nThe program reads the entries of the current directory, keeps only the regular files, collects their names into a list, sorts the list alphabetically, and prints each name on its own line.\n\nHow to test it yourself:\n1. Install Node.js from https://nodejs.org/.\n2. Save the code above to a file named `main.js`.\n3. Check that it compiles: `node --check main.js`.\n4. Run it: `node main.js`.\n5. Compare the output with the expected output shown above.","evidence":["response:write_program:list_files:javascript","algorithm_construction:meta_algorithm:problem_class_to_shared_ir_to_renderers_to_verification","algorithm_construction:active_surface:coding_catalog","algorithm_construction:stage:collect_corpus output=representative problem-class examples verifier=case-study corpus preserved","algorithm_construction:stage:derive_surfaces output=input and output surface ontology verifier=handler-specific surface recognition fixture","algorithm_construction:stage:extract_ir output=shared intermediate representation verifier=domain invariants preserved","algorithm_construction:stage:synthesize_operations output=recognizers, extractors, renderers, and validators verifier=operation composition invariants","algorithm_construction:stage:proj